## DESCRIPTION
## Implicit function theorem
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Implicit function theorem')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "parserPopUp.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

@lst = ["?", "Yes", "No", "Inconclusive"];
$mc_yes = PopUp(@lst, "Yes");
$mc_inc = PopUp(@lst, "Inconclusive");

BEGIN_PGML


Let [` F: \mathbb{R}^5 \to \mathbb{R}^3 `] be a [` C^1 `] map. Fix a point [` p \in \mathbb{R}^5 `]. You have calculated that

>>[` F(p) = \begin{bmatrix} 0\\0\\0 \end{bmatrix}, \quad DF(p) = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 3 \end{bmatrix} \quad \text{and} \quad \mathrm{rref}(DF(p)) = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \end{bmatrix} `].<<

Almost no calculations are needed for any part below.

1. Does the nonlinear system [` F(x)=0 `] locally define [` (x_1,x_2,x_3) `] as a [` C^1 `] function of [` (x_4,x_5) `]? [_]{$mc_inc}

2. Does the nonlinear system [` F(x)=0 `] locally define [` (x_1,x_2,x_4) `] as a [` C^1 `] function of [` (x_3,x_5) `]? [_]{$mc_yes}

3. Does the nonlinear system [` F(x)=0 `] locally define [` (x_2,x_3,x_4) `] as a [` C^1 `] function of [` (x_1,x_5) `]? [_]{$mc_yes}
END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();